Package: assignmentB2MadelineWoodley
Title: Calculate Grouped Means
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Madeline", "Woodley", email = "madeline.woodley@ubc.ca", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: This package contains a single function (and associated information), `groupedmeans()`, which allows users to efficiently group information within their dataframe (`data`) based on values in a variable (usually categorical) within their dataset (`var1`) and calculate the mean of values for another (numeric) variable (`var2`) in their dataset based on the `var1` groupings. The function returns a summary table with 'var1' and the associated grouped `var2` means. Note that the function is written to retain missing (NA) values for `var2`.
